From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:10:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 074/162] hjviewer: settings for what the build pins

U37: a build that fixes direct IP access, LAN discovery or the
insecure TLS fallback off (the pinned build, src/hjviewer.rs) leaves
their rows out instead of drawing them like live ones: 'Deny LAN
discovery' and 'Enable direct IP access' with its port in Security,
the TLS fallback switch in Network and on the phone, and the
Discovered tab, which no PC of such a build answers. The connection
box's tip then says only where to find the PC's ID, not upstream's
direct IPs, other servers and '/r'. For the fixed options that remain,
a box that cannot change has the faint border and its label the
disabled colour, a switch that cannot change a faint track and knob,
a fixed network row is dimmed as a locked one is, and
disabledTextColor is the theme's textDisabled. The decision for 1.8.2
was to hide, so no lock caption and no new empty_lan_tip.

U38: the phone settings' QR button is left out where the server
settings are hidden (the pinned build): a QR code only sets the
server, and its upstream screen is English. The camera and photo
prompts no longer come up that way.

U39: without RustDesk's printer driver adapter, which hjviewer builds
leave out, is-support-printer-driver is false; the Printer tab and
the 'Enable remote printer' permission are then left out instead of
saying that Windows 10 is needed. The check is on the Dart side with
the existing main_get_common key; it is also false before Windows 10,
where remote printing does not work either.

U56: _OptionCheckBox, _Radio and the RDP sharing row wrap their box
and label in MergeSemantics, so that Narrator and NVDA read the
setting's name with its state. Tapping the name still toggles it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
